# Playwright quick gates (mandatory before run)

Before proposing or running **any** Playwright command (`npx playwright test`, export/render smoke, trace viewer), run the **project-documented** stack health gates from repo root. **Do not** launch Playwright when gates fail — auth/timeouts are usually upstream (unhealthy API, broken web shell, missing seed, stale auth storage).

## Layout

Primary activation: umbraculum-class `apps/web/e2e/**` (same globs as rule `60-e2e-playwright-readmes`). Also fires on any `playwright.config.*` edit — then resolve suite root + README from `DEVELOPMENT.md` / `DEVELOPMENT-LOCAL.md` / `docs/TESTING.md` (do not invent paths).

| When this layout applies | Suite README (read first) |
|---|---|
| umbraculum-class `apps/web/e2e/**` | `apps/web/e2e/README.md` |
| other TS/JS consumers (config-only match) | path named in project docs — do not invent |

Platform test map (when present): `docs/TESTING.md` § L5.

## Procedure

Follow the **`playwright-runner-docs-gate`** skill — resolve compose services, health/login URLs, smoke script, and seed command from project docs; use its umbraculum-class examples only when that layout applies.

## Hard stops

- Project health probe (umbraculum-class example: `GET /api/health` → `{"ok":true}`) fails → fix the API/service named in project docs before Playwright.
- Project login/shell probe (umbraculum-class example: login page HTTP 200) fails → fix the web/app service before Playwright.
- Seed/fixture command from the E2E README not run when specs require seeded personas (umbraculum-class example: `seed:e2e`).
- After stack recovery: clear stale Playwright storage only at the path the project documents (umbraculum-class example: `apps/web/e2e/.auth/*.json`) if sessions fail despite healthy probes.
